# One subscription per line:  <pool-name> <url>
#
# The name namespaces that subscription's outbound tags and its pool files
# (50-pool-<name>-NN.json), so two subscriptions must never share one: -confdir
# merges by tag and a duplicate tag is silently overwritten, one node quietly
# gone. Re-running a pool removes that pool's old files first, so a subscription
# that shrank cannot leave stale chunks behind.
#
# Blank lines and # comments are ignored. Names may not contain whitespace.
#
# Repeated entries are dropped before the cap applies, so REFRESH_LIMIT buys
# distinct configurations rather than clones of one server.
#
# REFRESH_LIMIT (default 150) caps each one. That cap is per subscription and
# the observatory probes the TOTAL, concurrently, every interval - so four
# subscriptions at 150 is 600 nodes probed every 3 minutes, which is the point
# at which the balancer stops converging and looks like it is full of bad
# nodes. sub2xray prints the arithmetic when the total passes 200.

radikal_secure  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/0xRadikal/Free-v2ray-Configs/main/secure/configs.txt

# More sources, all verified to parse as plain URI lists (shadowmere is base64;
# the .html ones are plain text despite the extension). Uncomment what you want.
#
# ⚠ Together these are >13000 distinct nodes, and the observatory probes the
#   TOTAL every interval. Do NOT enable several at REFRESH_LIMIT=150. Since
#   --limit now samples at RANDOM rather than taking the head, a SMALL limit
#   across MANY subscriptions is strictly better than a large one across few:
#   every cycle walks a different slice, so the whole corpus gets covered over
#   an afternoon instead of the same 150 nodes being re-probed forever.
#   Nine subscriptions at REFRESH_LIMIT=25 is ~225 nodes per cycle, which is
#   about the budget one host converges on.

# The two large aggregators. Between them they carry most of what the others
# have, plus several thousand nodes nobody else mirrors.
#solispirit      https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SoliSpirit/v2ray-configs/main/all_configs.txt
#avencores26     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AvenCores/goida-vpn-configs/main/githubmirror/26.txt
#avencores12     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AvenCores/goida-vpn-configs/main/githubmirror/12.txt

# Small, and each carries a few dozen nodes the aggregators do not.
# shadowmere is worth its slot despite the size: it is all shadowsocks, so it
# fails differently from the vless-heavy lists above.
#openproxylist   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/roosterkid/openproxylist/refs/heads/main/V2RAY_RAW.txt
#arshiacomplus   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/arshiacomplus/v2rayExtractor/main/mix/sub.html
#shadowmere      https://shadowmere.xyz/api/b64sub/
#hidashimora     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Hidashimora/free-vpn-anti-rkn/main/configs/1.1.txt

